openmediavault-rustfs (8.0.1+rustfs1.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: RustFS S3 compatible object storage plugin for
    OpenMediaVault 8.x.
    - Bundles the upstream rustfs Linux binary (GNU build, amd64/arm64)
      downloaded from the upstream GitHub release at package build time
      and verified against the upstream SHA256SUMS; the version is pinned
      as the +rustfsX.Y.Z suffix of the package version so builds are
      reproducible.
    - runs as a native systemd service with the upstream unit hardening
      (Type=notify, ProtectHome, PrivateTmp, RestrictRealtime and so on).
    - The data directory is an OMV shared folder reference (single node
      single disk); the service cannot be started before the shared
      folder has been selected (form requiredIf, Salt guard and ctl
      guard), and installing or upgrading the package never starts it.
    - Access and secret keys are generated randomly at install time and
      can be rotated from the web interface; the default rustfsadmin
      credentials are never used.
    - Settings page with the API and console port, the console switch,
      the log level and a raw environment escape hatch, plus start,
      stop, restart, a log viewer, the generated /etc/default/rustfs
      preview and an 'Open console' button.
    - Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations included.

